// spec: an anonymous struct alternative holds data members alone (kovarex 2026-11-18, option 3A), one per declaration,
// each written as its creator's parameter is: a function, a static member, a type or a bit-field in it is an error (name
// the struct to give it one), as are `int x, y;` and an array. design.md 8.5
// error: typed_union_anonymous_struct_alternative_errors.kpp:13: error: the anonymous struct of the alternative Sized holds data members alone: a function is not one (name the struct to give it one)
// error: typed_union_anonymous_struct_alternative_errors.kpp:14: error: the anonymous struct of the alternative Counted holds data members alone: a static member is not one (name the struct to give it one)
// error: typed_union_anonymous_struct_alternative_errors.kpp:15: error: the anonymous struct of the alternative Bits holds data members alone: a bit-field is not one (name the struct to give it one)
// error: typed_union_anonymous_struct_alternative_errors.kpp:16: error: the anonymous struct of the alternative Pair declares one member per declaration (its creator takes them as parameters)
// error: typed_union_anonymous_struct_alternative_errors.kpp:17: error: the anonymous struct of the alternative Listed has a member its creator cannot take as written: write its type before its name (std::Array for an array)
union enum Action : u8
{
  {
    {Close, struct { int a; }},
    {Sized, struct { int b; int size() const { return this.b; } }},
    {Counted, struct { static int count; int c; }},
    {Bits, struct { u8 low : 4; }},
    {Pair, struct { int x, y; }},
    {Listed, struct { int values[3]; }}
  }
};
int main()
{
  return 0;
}
